From: Armada contributors <noreply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: dt-platdev: blocklist Qualcomm Eliza

Eliza uses qcom-cpufreq-hw. Adding static CPU OPP bandwidth tables for
EPSS L3 makes cpufreq-dt-platdev instantiate the generic driver as well.
On the Duo this logs a failed registration with -EEXIST because the
hardware driver already owns the policies. Blocklist Eliza like the
other Qualcomm platforms using the hardware driver.

---
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -153,6 +153,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "nvidia,tegra234", },
 
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,apq8096", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8909", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8996", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998", },
